@startuml
title AD-02 - Find and Filter a Mobility Hub

|Actor|
start
:Select Find a Mobility Hub;

|System / Controller|
:Display search and filter options;

|Actor|
:Choose location search method;

if (Use current location?) then (Yes)
    |System / Controller|
    :Request current location;

    if (Location available?) then (Yes)
        :Receive current coordinates;
    else (No)
        |Actor|
        :Enter location manually;

        |System / Controller|
        :Validate entered location;

        if (Location valid?) then (Yes)
            :Accept manual location;
        else (No)
            |Actor|
            :Correct location information;
            |System / Controller|
            :Validate corrected location;
        endif
    endif

else (No)
    |Actor|
    :Enter location manually;

    |System / Controller|
    :Validate entered location;

    if (Location valid?) then (Yes)
        :Accept manual location;
    else (No)
        |Actor|
        :Correct location information;
        |System / Controller|
        :Validate corrected location;
    endif
endif

|Actor|
:Select required services and filters;
:Submit search request;

|System / Controller|
:Validate search criteria;

|Database|
:Search Mobility Hubs;
:Retrieve matching Hub records;

|System / Controller|
if (Matching Hubs found?) then (Yes)
    :Prepare matching results;

    |Actor|
    :View matching Mobility Hubs;
    :Select a Mobility Hub;
    :Open Hub details;
    stop

else (No)
    |Actor|
    :View no-results message;
    :Change location or filters;

    |System / Controller|
    :Process updated search criteria;

    |Database|
    :Search Mobility Hubs again;
    :Return updated results;

    |System / Controller|
    :Display updated results;

    |Actor|
    :Review search results;
    stop
endif

@enduml